<title>USA: Bradlees Q1 shr loss $2.81 vs loss $4.71.</title>
<headline>Bradlees Q1 shr loss $2.81 vs loss $4.71.</headline>
<dateline>BRAINTREE, Mass. 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>BRADLEES INC AND SUBSIDIARIES</p>
<p>			   (Operating as Debtor-In-Possession)</p>
<p>		   CONDENSED CONSOLIDATED STATEMENTS OF OPERATIONS</p>
<p>					   (Unaudited)</p>
<p>		   (Dollars in thousands except per share amounts)</p>
<p>						   13 Weeks Ended</p>
<p>					     5/3/97	   5/4/96</p>
<p>    Total sales			  $276,838	  $349,891</p>
<p>    Leased sales			    9,467	    12,188</p>
<p>    Net sales			     267,371	   337,703</p>
<p>    Net loss			    ($31,993)	 ($53,746)</p>
<p>    Net loss per share		  ($2.81)	   ($4.71)</p>
<p>NOTE: Average shares 11.391 million shares outstanding for the first quarter of 1997 and 11.411 million for the same period a year ago.</p>
<p>The company said ineventories were about $10 million below plan at the end of the quarter.  The company said inventories were tightly controlled in the face of a sales shortfall.</p>
</text>
